.TH PDBU 1 "2026" "pdbu 1.0.0" "PDBU Manual"
.SH NAME
pdbu \- Personal Directory Backup Utility: back up and restore a home directory with rsync
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B pdbu
[\fIGLOBAL OPTIONS\fR] \fICOMMAND\fR [\fIARGS\fR]...
.PP
.B pdbu-gui
.SH DESCRIPTION
PDBU creates a one-to-one mirrored backup of a user's home directory using
.BR rsync (1),
to a local LUKS-encrypted external drive or a remote host over SSH, and can
restore from either. It provides both this command-line interface and a
GTK4 graphical interface (\fBpdbu-gui\fR); both use the same backup and
restore engine, so behaviour is identical between them.
.SH GLOBAL OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
Show detailed output.
.TP
.BR \-q ", " \-\-quiet
Only show errors.
.TP
.BR \-y ", " \-\-yes
Assume yes to confirmation prompts (required for non-interactive use of
destructive operations).
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B status \fR[\fB\-\-json\fR]
Show a dashboard-style summary: last successful backup, schedule, drive and
SSH status, recent operations.
.TP
.B backup \fR[\fB\-\-drive\-a\fR|\fB\-\-drive\-b\fR|\fB\-\-ssh\fR] [\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR]
Run a backup. Without a destination flag, PDBU uses the recommended
(alternating) drive.
.TP
.B restore \fB\-\-source\fR {drive\-a,drive\-b,ssh} [\fB\-\-path\fR \fIP\fR ...] [\fB\-\-destination\fR \fIDIR\fR] [\fB\-\-conflict\fR \fIMODE\fR] [\fB\-\-mirror\-delete\fR] [\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR]
Restore all or selected content from a backup. \fB\-\-conflict\fR is one of
\fBoverwrite\fR, \fBskip\fR, \fBnewer\fR, \fBask\fR, \fBrename\fR.
.TP
.B drives \fR[\fB\-\-json\fR]
Show configured/connected backup drive status and the recommended next
drive to alternate to.
.TP
.B history \fR[\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-\-limit\fR \fIN\fR] [\fB\-\-type\fR \fITYPE\fR]
Show past backup/restore operations.
.TP
.B logs \fR[\fIOPERATION_ID\fR] [\fB\-\-tail\fR \fIN\fR]
Show the log file for one operation, or list recent operations and their
log paths.
.TP
.B verify \fR[\fB\-\-drive\-a\fR|\fB\-\-drive\-b\fR|\fB\-\-ssh\fR] [\fB\-\-json\fR]
Compare source and destination without modifying either.
.TP
.B config \fR[\fB\-\-edit\fR] [\fB\-\-show\fR] [\fB\-\-json\fR]
Show or edit the TOML configuration file.
.TP
.B schedule \fR[\fB\-\-interval\fR \fIVALUE\fR]
Show or set the backup reminder interval (e.g. \fB7d\fR, \fB24h\fR).
.TP
.B reminder\-check
Check whether a backup is due and show a desktop notification if so. Used
by the \fBpdbu\-reminder.timer\fR systemd user timer; safe to run manually.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
General error.
.TP
.B 2
Usage error (bad arguments).
.TP
.B 3
A confirmation was required and not given.
.TP
.B 4
A safety check refused the operation (dangerous path, identity mismatch, etc).
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/pdbu/config.toml
Configuration.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/pdbu/history.sqlite3
Operation history database.
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/pdbu/logs/
Per-operation log files.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR rsync (1),
.BR ssh (1),
.BR cryptsetup (8)
